{"is_error":false,"duration_api_ms":340573,"num_turns":25,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"b5533633-2623-4ad9-98f1-ecf532e99e83","total_cost_usd":2.8826454999999997,"usage":{"input_tokens":37,"cache_creation_input_tokens":124729,"cache_read_input_tokens":1996141,"output_tokens":25484,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":124729,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1074,"cache_read_input_tokens":139465,"cache_creation_input_tokens":532,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":532},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5":{"inputTokens":37,"outputTokens":25484,"cacheReadInputTokens":1996141,"cacheCreationInputTokens":124729,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":2.8826454999999997,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5","provider":"firstParty"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"Done. Commit `574a400` contains only the state file — my earlier three-file `--stat` was a misread of my own command (it compared against the working tree, not the commit).\n\n## What happened\n\nThis was Unit 2 of the `diagnostics-workflow` task, in Discovery mode. Codex asked me to run the qualification half of `/develop-ai-resource` and settle *which* mechanism to build, before anything gets built. I checked eight premises against the repository, ran the qualification, and handed back to Codex. No target file was changed.\n\n**The verdict: improve the two commands you already have.** Repair two broken contracts inside the existing `/resolve-repo-problem` → `/resolve-incident` path. Do not build a new command, do not merge the two, do not retire either, do not touch the router.\n\n**The finding that decided it.** The brief assumed one operator-facing front door was missing. It is not missing. The Work Loop v2 router *is* the front door — you describe the problem in ordinary language and it returns exactly one owner, with both fault commands indexed under distinct triggers. You only have to pick a command yourself if you skip the router and type a command name, and that is true of all 26 indexed commands, not a defect of this pair. So merging the two would buy nothing at intake, while breaking 25 project symlinks and a frozen check in the acceptance harness.\n\n**The two real defects, both reproduced today by inspection, not recalled:**\n\n1. `/resolve-repo-problem` tells you it passes its triage notes forward to `/resolve-incident`. It does not. Searching `resolve-incident.md` for `NOTES_PATH`, `triage notes` and `notes path` returns nothing, so the fix command throws the notes away and investigates the problem a second time.\n2. `/resolve-incident` aborts at its very first step in any project repository. It looks for `ai-resources/` *inside* the current repo, but `ai-resources` and `projects` are siblings. It is deployed to 25 project folders and works in none of them.\n\n**One thing Codex must not skip.** Both fixes edit shared command files, which `docs/protected-zones.md` protects. That makes the next unit take one risk-aware Codex review **before** implementation. I did not run it and did not treat it as optional.\n\n**Two items I pushed out of scope, with reasons.** The `No commit` rule in both commands contradicts your workspace rules and the Work Loop core — that is a policy decision across three authorities and belongs to you, not to a contract repair. The scanner-twin disagreement is untracked content sitting only in the main checkout, so it is not reachable from this branch at all.\n\n**One limitation worth knowing:** your two SOP drafts are chat attachments, not repository files. I could not read them. Their content reached this verdict only through the research map's summary of them.\n\nCodex now decides whether to open the Implementation unit on the boundary I wrote, or stop.","ttft_ms":2128,"ttft_stream_ms":1373,"time_to_request_ms":65,"type":"result","duration_ms":344790,"uuid":"67ca403a-a0ce-48ce-903d-7f9919871a74"}
